# Nougat OCR stub — BVBRC-90 Kavvas et al. 2018

**Status:** Nougat OCR was NOT run on this paper. This file is a provenance stub explaining why
and pointing at the actual extraction sources that were used.

## Why Nougat was not run
- The paper is open-access CC BY 4.0 with a native-text HTML/XML rendering at PubMed Central
  (PMC6193043). Extracting text from that source is one `curl` + `readability` pass; running
  Nougat's 350M ViT-based OCR is unnecessary overhead.
- The paper's data payload (which is what the replication actually consumed) is in the
  supplementary XLSX + PDF files distributed on Springer's static-content CDN:
  - `41467_2018_6634_MOESM1_ESM.pdf` (supplementary info narrative, 5.38 MB)
  - `41467_2018_6634_MOESM4_ESM.xlsx` (MI/χ²/ANOVA top-40 per drug)
  - `41467_2018_6634_MOESM5_ESM.xlsx` (SVM-SGD selected alleles)
  - `41467_2018_6634_MOESM7_ESM.xlsx` (epistatic interactions)
  - `41467_2018_6634_MOESM9_ESM.xlsx` (2000-allele AMR panel)
  - `41467_2018_6634_MOESM8_ESM.xlsx` (co-occurrence tables — Springer 403)
- Structured XLSX + native-text PDF are strictly better inputs than OCR'd markdown for a
  quantitative replication.

## If a future run wants Nougat markdown of the paper
```
# Native-text PDF (preferred; no OCR needed):
curl -L -o /tmp/kavvas2018.pdf \
  https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-018-06634-y.pdf
nougat /tmp/kavvas2018.pdf -o extraction/ --markdown
mv extraction/kavvas2018.mmd extraction/nougat.mmd
```
Or use the PMC XML directly (fastest, cleanest):
```
curl -L -o extraction/kavvas2018.pmc.xml \
  https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6193043/?report=classic&format=xml
```

## What "text" this replication actually consumed
- **Paper text:** parsed inline from PMC HTML during report drafting (headline claims, Table 1
  known-gene list, Table 2 new-gene list, epistatic-pair callouts, AUC>0.80 claim).
- **Structured data:** supplementary XLSX sheets parsed with `openpyxl` (MOESM4/5/7/9).
- **Reference sequences:** NCBI E-utils `efetch` for 6 canonical AMR-gene RefSeqs (katG, pncA,
  rpoB, gyrA, inhA, rpsL).

No Nougat-derived text was needed for any of the C1–C7 tests. This stub exists so future
audits do not mistake absence-of-Nougat for absence-of-extraction.
